title: Campaign ending
new-page: true

= [? if terminal_reason = "Majles rejection": 15 March 1951 ?][? if terminal_reason != "Majles rejection": 20 March 1951 ?]

**[+ ending_name +]**

[? if terminal_reason = "": The {!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!}
has approved the nationalization principle. ?]
[? if terminal_reason = "Majles rejection": The oil committee recommended
nationalization, but the principle failed to command the required support in
the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}. ?]
[? if terminal_reason = "Senate rejection": The
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} approved the
principle, but the {!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!}
did not complete the constitutional sequence. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "Majles rejection": Of the
[+ majles_attending_members +] members present and entitled to
vote, [+ nationalization_majles_support +] supported nationalization,
[+ nationalization_majles_conditional +] remained conditional, and
[+ nationalization_majles_opposed +] opposed it. The proposal fell
[+ 0 - nationalization_majles_support_gap +] votes short. The campaign's
returns and credential victories therefore did not become enough firm
commitments on oil. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "Senate rejection": Lower-chamber success did not
survive the passage to the upper chamber. Of the
[+ senate_attending_members +] senators present and entitled
to vote, [+ nationalization_senate_support +] supported nationalization,
[+ nationalization_senate_conditional +] remained conditional, and
[+ nationalization_senate_opposed +] opposed it. The proposal fell
[+ 0 - nationalization_senate_support_gap +] votes short. The parliamentary
record, {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Crown{!</span>!} relationship,
and cross-chamber appeal had not persuaded enough senators to complete the
constitutional sequence. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "" and ending_name = "A Constitutional Coalition": The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} arrives as more than a temporary oil alliance. Its component organizations remain distinct, but they have enough trust, constitutional credibility, and parliamentary capacity to keep negotiating a common course after the vote. Nationalization is therefore paired with a plausible coalition for the institutional struggle that follows. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "" and ending_name = "A Parliamentary Vanguard": A disciplined group inside the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} has carried the principle farther than the coalition's wider organization can comfortably sustain. Parliamentary leverage is the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}'s strongest instrument, but it rests on a narrower base: either internal durability or public organization has not kept pace with chamber success. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "" and ending_name = "A Movement of the Streets": The campaign reaches the vote with its clearest strength outside the chambers. Meetings, press, and organizational networks have created a broad public force, even though constitutional or parliamentary consolidation remains less secure. The movement can exert pressure; converting that pressure into durable institutional control is the unresolved task. ?]

[? if terminal_reason = "" and ending_name = "A Fragile Nationalization": The principle passes, but the organization carrying it remains vulnerable. Coalition relations, constitutional standing, parliamentary leverage, and public machinery have not combined into one dependable base. The victory has been reached without settling who can defend or administer its consequences. ?]

= Four dimensions

* Coalition durability: [+ ending_coalition +] / 100
* Constitutional legitimacy: [+ ending_legitimacy +] / 100
* Parliamentary capacity: [+ ending_parliament +] / 100
* Public organization: [+ ending_public +] / 100

{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} support for
nationalization: [+ nationalization_majles_support +] /
[+ nationalization_majles_threshold +] required

[+ nationalization_majles_conditional +] members remained conditional and
[+ nationalization_majles_opposed +] opposed the principle among
[+ majles_attending_members +] attending members entitled to
vote.

