among [+ senate_attending_members +] attending senators
entitled to vote. ?]

Release: [+ release_version +]

= Causal recap

**Advisers at the final vote — [+ active_advisor_names +].**

These were the figures whose counsel the opposition had kept closest. Other
eligible allies remained part of the coalition, but did not shape its final
preparations as directly.

**{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} structure —
[+ front_structure +].**

[? if front_structure = "Narrow constitutional alliance": You kept the common program narrow enough for unlike organizations to defend together. That strengthened a public constitutional rule while leaving local machinery primarily with the components. ?]
[? if front_structure = "Loose coordination committee": You protected the autonomy of cooperating organizations and improved their willingness to share information. The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} remained dependent on several chains of authority whenever it needed to act as one. ?]
[? if front_structure = "Membership-based coalition": You invested in a common membership organization that could reach supporters directly. The same structure produced arguments over control among organizations that feared absorption. ?]

**The Tehran rerun.**

[? if election_strategy = "Concentrated Tehran slate": You concentrated scarce organizers behind a visible Tehran slate, strengthening electoral identity more than nationwide documentation. ?]
[? if election_strategy = "Monitoring and credential record": You prioritized a record of returns and interference, giving the later credential campaign stronger evidence and procedure. ?]
[? if election_strategy = "Slate with selective monitoring": You paid for a mixed approach: a recognizable slate accompanied by selective monitoring, without maximizing either concentration or coverage. ?]

**The credential campaign.**

[? if credentials_strategy = "Case-by-case procedural challenge": You treated each credential as its own constitutional case, building procedural standing without assuming that every returned ally was already usable. ?]
[? if credentials_strategy = "Coordinated National Front group": You emphasized the returned deputies as a visible {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} group, turning a small cohort into a clearer parliamentary force. ?]
[? if credentials_strategy = "Deputy liaison and procedural outreach": You worked through liaison and persuasion beyond the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}, exchanging some internal simplicity for a wider parliamentary network. ?]

**Parliamentary position — [+ majles_returns_recorded +] returns recorded,
[+ majles_credentials_approved +] approved credentials, and
[+ majles_attending_members +] members present and entitled to vote.**

Campaign work strengthened candidacies only where a genuine contest was
possible. The later credential campaign could defend a returned deputy, but
could not create a return; only approved members who attended could vote.

**The oil case.**

[? if oil_terms_position = "Constitutional control": Your baseline remained a general demand for constitutionally accountable national control. ?]
[? if oil_terms_position = "Term-by-term national control": Recurring committee work separated ownership, operations, marketing, compensation, finance, personnel, and review before defining an acceptable minimum. ?]
[? if oil_terms_position = "Documented term-by-term rejection": The rejection campaign compared the agreement's provisions directly and explained why improved payments alone did not answer the demand for national control. ?]

**The confrontation with {!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!}.**

[? if razmara_response = "Parliamentary term-by-term rebuttal": You answered {!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!} primarily through the parliamentary record, strengthening the committee case and its procedural credibility. ?]
[? if razmara_response = "Public nationalization campaign": You carried the confrontation into a more direct public campaign, expanding mandate while sharpening resistance from the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Crown{!</span>!}. ?]
[? if razmara_response = "Joint parliamentary and public response": You spent scarce resources to coordinate the chamber case with public explanation, building a broader response without fully specializing in either route. ?]

[? if nationalization_approved_majles = 1: **The approach to the
{!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!}.** ?]

[? if nationalization_approved_majles = 1 and senate_strategy = "Institutional record": You sent senators the
committee and {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}
record, asking the upper chamber to complete the institutional sequence. ?]
[? if nationalization_approved_majles = 1 and senate_strategy = "Public briefings": You carried the public campaign
into the final days, asking senators to answer a demand already moving through
meetings and newspapers. ?]
[? if nationalization_approved_majles = 1 and senate_strategy = "Cross-chamber constitutional case": Deputies and
senators received one constitutional argument joining the committee record,
the lower-chamber vote, and the principle of national control. ?]

**Organizational resources — [+ resources +] remaining; [+ dues +] annual
income.**

[? if resource_strain_months > 0: For the final
[+ resource_strain_months +] months, an empty treasury forced editors and
local organizers to let routine work lapse. ?]
[? if resource_strain_months = 0 and resources > 0: The campaign reached the
vote with money still available for printing, travel, meetings, or legal work. ?]

[? if press_project = "Constitutional editorial network": Friendly papers
ended the campaign leading with representative government and lawful
procedure. ?]
[? if press_project = "Oil dossier network": Friendly papers ended the
campaign explaining the disputed oil provisions in detail. ?]
[? if press_project = "Plural editorial compact": Friendly papers continued
to state a common demand in distinct political voices. ?]
[? if press_project = "Fatemi editorial campaign":
{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Hossein Fatemi{!</span>!} had drawn the
friendly editors into a common public campaign. ?]

[? if committee_model = "Shared local committees": Local work rested on shared
committees paid from the common purse. ?]
[? if committee_model = "Autonomous component organizers": Each component
retained command of its own organizers, leaving joint work dependent on
negotiation among parallel networks. ?]

[? if credential_project = "Case-by-case files": Credential work ended with
separate documentary files for the contested returns. ?]
[? if credential_project = "Floor coordination": Returned opposition deputies
had divided the speaking work for credential debates. ?]

[? if oil_project = "Term-by-term comparison": The parliamentary team had
compared the agreement provision by provision. ?]
[? if oil_project = "Cross-faction majority": The parliamentary team had
concentrated on language that supporters from several tendencies could defend. ?]
[? if oil_project = "Procedural commission record": Deputies and editors had
a common account distinguishing documented, disputed, and unknown provisions. ?]
[? if oil_project = "Makki committee examination":
{!<span class="term term-makki">!}Hossein Makki{!</span>!} had pressed the
committee to test the agreement against the demand for national control. ?]

[? if last_project_setback = "Court pressure on constituency work": The
{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!} had most recently
obstructed constituency organization. ?]
[? if last_project_setback = "Court pressure on parliamentary work": The
{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!} had most recently
obstructed parliamentary work. ?]
[? if last_project_setback = "Coalition procedure challenged": The coalition's
agreed procedure had most recently been challenged by its own component
organizations. ?]
[? if last_project_setback = "Joint work weakened by coalition coordination":
The latest joint effort had lost force because component leaders could not
carry the same decision through their organizations. ?]
[? if last_project_setback = "Unfunded routine work reduced press and local organizational capacity":
Earlier in the campaign, the most recent recorded setback came when an empty
treasury forced press and local work to contract. Later income or fundraising
may have restored the balance shown above. ?]

**{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Crown{!</span>!} relationship:**
[? if shah_relation < 35: hostile. ?]
[? if shah_relation >= 35 and shah_relation < 65: guarded. ?]
[? if shah_relation >= 65: workable. ?]

**{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Crown{!</span>!} resistance:**
[? if shah_resistance < 35: limited. ?]
[? if shah_resistance >= 35 and shah_resistance < 65: substantial. ?]
[? if shah_resistance >= 65: severe. ?]

